BT /F2 17 Tf 54 748 Td (Dijkstra's Shortest Path Algorithm) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 723 Td (Topic: Greedy    File: g5.pdf) Tj ET
0.6 w 54 711 m 558 711 l S
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 692 Td (PROBLEM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 678 Td (Find shortest-path distances from a source vertex in a graph whose edge weights are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 665 Td (    non-negative.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 645 Td (GREEDY CHOICE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 631 Td (Repeatedly finalize the unvisited vertex with the smallest tentative distance, then) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 618 Td (    relax its outgoing edges.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 598 Td (ALGORITHM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 584 Td (Set dist[source] = 0 and all other distances to infinity. Use a min-priority queue; for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 571 Td (    each edge u->v, update dist[v] if dist[u] + weight\(u,v\) is smaller.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 551 Td (EXAMPLE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 537 Td (If S-A costs 2, S-B costs 7, and A-B costs 1, the shortest distance from S to B is 3 via) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 524 Td (    A.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 504 Td (COMPLEXITY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 490 Td (With adjacency lists and a binary heap: O\(\(V + E\) log V\) time and O\(V + E\) graph) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 477 Td (    storage.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 457 Td (IMPORTANT) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 443 Td (Dijkstra is not correct for graphs with negative edge weights. Consider Bellman-Ford for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 430 Td (    those cases.) Tj ET
